==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|pe}}

===Etymology===
Derives from the name of the Baltic deity of thunder, compare Lithuanian [[Perkūnas]]. The meaning was changed to devil by priests after the introduction of Christianity.

===Noun===
'''perkele'''

# The [[Devil]], [[Satan]]
# [[devil]]

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-hame|perkel}}

====Synonyms====
*[[paholainen]]
*[[piru]]

===Interjection===
'''perkele!'''

# {{vulgar|lang=fi}} an interjection said by someone for example annoyed or surprised
#: '''''Perkele''' se on hidas!''
#:: '''Damn''' it's slow!

===Adjective===
'''perkele'''

# {{vulgar|lang=fi}} an [[intensifier]]
#:''Se on '''perkeleen''' ruma.''
#:: It's so '''bloody''' ugly.

